    "incipit": "ተብህለ፡ ከመ፡ ሀሎ፡ አሐዱ፡ ብእሲ፡ ሐፃቤ፡ አልባስ፡ ወእንዘ፡ የሐፅብ፡ ልብሰ፡ መጽአ፡ አሐዱ፡ ብእሲ፡ ወሜጠ፡ ማየ፡ እንተ፡ ካልእ፡ ፍኖት",
    "manuscript_count": 142,
    "translations": [
      {
        "author": "Rowan Williams",
        "text": "<p>The Miracles of Our Lady Mary, the Holy Twofold Virgin Theotokos</p><p> </p><p>May the blessing of her prayers be with us. Amen.</p><p>Now we shall relate to you how Our Lady Mary is much more honourable than her relatives, and indeed the whole world, so that you may discern the greatness of her Nativity.[2]</p><p>And it came to pass that Satan entered the hearts of the people of Israel. They convened a council[3] and plotted together, saying, ‘Have you not heard[4] that there is nothing of profit to you? For behold, Anne and Joachim have risen up against us. They will rule over us,[5] and we shall be their slaves.[6] As all of you are aware, you have seen what Anne did when she conceived. When Samser son of tabeq died at the fort of Jericho and we were taking him to the tomb, Anne came into the middle of the road and took hold of the casket, weeping because he was the brother of her father, and she loved him very much. At that moment, he arose and spoke these words to her, saying, “Salutation to you, O Mother of the Sun of righteousness!” Then he said to her, “I have heard an Angel saying concerning Mary, who is to be born,[7] ‘She is the Mother of the Creator of Heaven and Earth,[8] He Who created humans and animals, the visible and the invisible’.” Now, O people of Israel, why do you sleep? And why do you remain silent concerning Anne and Joachim, who are mere mortals, and concerning she who was born of them?[9] As she is in the Temple this very day!’ When they heard this, they said to one another, ‘Let us go to the Temple by night and kill her. If we leave her in the city, she will call all people to herself.’</p><p>At midnight the next day, they rose up and entered the Temple, and there they found[10] Angels ascending and descending and giving praise with sweet songs which cannot be expressed. They sang, ‘Holy God,[11] holy Mighty, holy Living Immortal, Who was born of the holy Virgin Mary; have mercy on us, Lord. Holy God, holy Mighty, holy Living Immortal, Who rests in His Saints and is glorified by the humble!’ And in the Temple, all the gates were ablaze with burning fire. When they saw this, they were put to shame and turned back.</p><p>May her prayers and blessings be with her servant Halawi Krestos to the ages of ages. Amen.</p>"
      }
    ]
