        "text": "<p>A miracle performed by Our Lady Mary. May her prayers, her blessings, and the mercy of her Son be with us, amen.</p><p>Holy Father Aba Abraham the Syrian was the sixty-second patriarch of the city of Alexandria.</p><p>During the patriarchate of this father Abraham, Muʿizz was the caliph of Misr and had a general who was Jewish, but observed Muslim customs. That general had a Jewish friend who would always come before the king with him and they would speak together. After that Jewish man found favor with the king alongside his friend, the king’s general, he made a request of the king. He said to the king: “I have a request for you, bring me the patriarch so that I can debate with him.” </p><p>The king sent a messenger to bring Aba Abraham along with Aba Severus ibn al-Muqaffa, the bishop of Ashmunin. [Having arrived at the king’s court] They debated with that Jewish man and won, putting him to shame.</p><p>When the king saw this victory, he rejoiced and honored the patriarch and those who were with him. They returned to their homes peacefully. However, the general with his Jewish friend due to their great embarrassment sought a way to defeat the patriarch and all the Christians.</p><p>One day, the general came to the king, saying: “My dear lord, I assure you that the Christians lack faith, because it is said in their Gospels: ‘If you have faith as small as a mustard seed, then you could say to this mountain: ‘Move and fall into the sea’, and it would move’.”</p><p>When the king heard this from the general, he sent a messenger and brought back the patriarch Aba Abraham. The king said to him: “What do you all say about the statement in your Gospel which says: ‘If you have faith as small as a mustard seed, then you could say to this mountain: ‘Move’, and it would move’?”</p><p>The patriarch answered him: “Yes, the Holy Gospel really does say that.”</p><p>Then the king said: “Look, you have thousands and tens of thousands of believers in your faith. I want you to bring one of your best so that he can reveal this miracle by his hand.”</p><p>When Aba Abraham heard this challenge, he was terrified and fearful. He answered the king: “Give me three days.”</p><p>The king answered: “Let it be just as you said.”</p><p>Then the patriarch departed from the king’s presence and gathered the bishops, the clergy, and the monks who were close by. They met for three days and three nights in the Muʿallaqa church in Misr, the church of Our Lady Mary, the Twofold Holy Virgin. They were fasting, praying and beseeching God. On the morning of the third day, Our Lady Mary, the Twofold Holy Virgin, the Mother of God, appeared to the patriarch with a radiant and joyful face. She said to him: “What has happened to you?”</p><p>He answered her: “You know what has happened to me.”</p><p>She said to him: “Do not be afraid, because I have now received your tears that you have poured out in my church. So now get up and go to the Iron Gate that leads you to the market. You will find [there] a man who is carrying a vessel full of water on his shoulder. He has one eye. Grab him, for he will perform this miracle for you. The name of this man is Simon, who sows shoes. For he gouged out his own eye, in accordance with the command of my beloved son, the Lord Christ.”</p><p>So the patriarch got up, quickly went [to the gate] and found that man. He said to him: “Show mercy to the Christians.”</p><p>Abraham told Simon about how Our Lady Mary, the Twofold Holy Virgin appeared to him and told him about Simon. Then Simon bowed down, saying: “Forgive me, my dear father, because I am a sinner and a transgressor. I am unable to do what you have told me, unless it is the will of God. In that case, let it be by the prayer of Our Lady, the Twofold Holy Virgin. And, Abraham, may your prayer help the Christians. Moreover, my dear father, I am begging you not to reveal my actions to anyone, because I am unable to bear the glory of this world. Rather, I will tell you the actions to take. Go out to the mountain that the king has told you about, take with you your clergy and your people. Also take with you the Gospel manuscripts and the crosses, the censers and candles. Let the king stay with his soldiers and all his people off to one side. You and your people [should stay] on the other side. I will stand behind you, in the midst of the people and no one will recognize me. Beseech God and cry out forty one times saying ‘Kyrie Eleison’, which means ‘God have mercy on us’. Then command the people to be silent. Then bow and have them bow with you. I will bow with you as well. Do this three times while making the sign of the saving cross, facing that mountain.’”</p><p>After the patriarch heard this, he brought together the bishops, the clergy, the monks, the people and the faithful believers. Then they went to the king. The king and all his troops, as well as the people of Misr and Cairo went out to that mountain. The patriarch Aba Abraham and the believers stood on one side and the king and his troops, as well as all the people stood on the other side. After this, the patriarch along with Simon and the faithful Christians prayed for a long while: “Dear Lord, have mercy on us.”</p><p>They bowed three times and each time they bowed, the father patriarch raised up his eyes to the heavens, making the sign of the cross over the mountain. The mountain moved, lifting up into the air in front of all the people. When the patriarch and the faithful Christians bowed down, that mountain came back down into its place. They did this three times. </p><p>When the king and all the Muslims saw this sign and wonder, they were greatly amazed and terrified.</p><p>May your prayers and your blessings be with us, forever and ever, amen.</p>"
