    "id": "35-A",
    "title": "Dabra Metmaq's Annual Apparition: Part 1: Dabra Metmaq's church and how Jesus promises the Virgin Mary that it would be built in her honor [expanded part of 35A, not 35B]",
    "incipit": "ወሶበ ፡ ፈጸመ ፡ እግዚእነ ፡ ዘሎቱ ፡ ስብሐት ፡ ሐኒፀ ፡ ቤተ ፡ መቅደስ ፡ ዘእሙ ፡ ቅድስት ፤ ካዕበ ፡ ይቤላ ፡ ለወላዲቱ ፡ ድንግል ፡ ከመ ፡ በደኃሪ ፡ መዋዕል ፡ ይትሐነፅ ፡ ቤተ ፡ ክርስቲያን ፡ ዐቢይ ፡ በስምየ ፡ ወበስምኪ ።",
    "manuscript_count": 102,
    "translations": [
      {
        "author": "Rowan Williams",
        "text": "<p>The Miracles of Our Lady Mary, the Holy Twofold Virgin Theotokos</p><br><p>May her prayers and blessings be with us to the ages of ages. Amen.</p><br><p>When Our praiseworthy Lord had completed the construction of His holy Mother’s sanctuary, He spoke to His Virgin Birth-giver again, saying, ‘In the latter days, a large church will be built in My Name and in yours.[1] 3It will be a monastery of Monks. 4Miracles will be made manifest within it.[2] Great power will be revealed to every nation, each according to their own language, 6and all people will see it, both believers and Muslims. 7It will be a memorial of My Advent to the world and My Incarnation from you for the salvation of Adam and his children. 8And from[3] the twenty-first to the twenty-fifth day of Genbot, you will appear in that monastery which will be built in your name, 9and I shall command the pure Archangels Michael and Gabriel to stand,[4] one at your left and the other at your right. 10I shall glorify My dwelling in your womb, 11and homage will be paid to My Incarnation from you. 12I shall have all the Martyrs minister to you, all those who were martyred for My Name and bore My suffering in their bodies and followed the footsteps in which I delight.[5] 13The Jews who crucified Me will also go to that holy place and stay within it, 14and they will bow down in honour of you.[6] 15And everyone there will see others as a brother sees his brother, a father his son, friends their friends, and lovers their beloved; so that all people may know that you are exalted above the heavenly and more honourable than the earthly. 16When anyone has faith and[7] supplicates you in My Name, one of the Saints or the Martyrs will do what they desire for them. 17And others of the faithful who have departed in the Orthodox Faith will come to you; those who make supplication of you will see them,[8] 18and whoever sees them will rejoice at the sight of them.’ </p><br><p> Now when the holy church was built in the name of His Virgin Mother,[9] in the place concerning which we have just made mention, this sign was made manifest as a testimony to the end of the age, as the True One, He Who knows no falsehood, had promised His Mother.[10] 20Many Monks gathered there, 21and it became a large monastery. 22It was called Dayr al-Maghtis[11] 23and made known throughout the whole world. 24On the eve of the feast day, they come from every region and country. 25Every year, from the twenty-first to the twenty-fifth of Genbot: Copts, Ethiopians, Armenians, Alexandrians, Maroneians, Kurds,[12] Franks, Romans, Lystrians,[13] Persians and Greeks all come from east and west to this monastery, and they see miracles and wonders because of Our Lady Mary. 26Her apparition[14] is made manifest in the dome of the church, 27and afterwards, all who see it tell the people of their own country about it. </p><br> <p>May her prayers and blessings be with us to the ages of ages. Amen.</p"
      }
    ]
