        "text": "<p>A miracle of Mary. </p><br><p>Listen, my fathers and brothers, about the sign and wonder that she performed in the land of Fares. </p><br><p>She entered the land of France and found a man whose foot was stone. Mary entered the church and that man went to her. He concealed his foot with a cloth so that the people would not recognize him. He was weeping and lamenting without rest, night and day. </p><br><p>Every day he loved to journey to that church. The entire church was adorned with gold, precious gems, and jacinth. Whenever he returned to that church, he would [accidentally] crush the gold and precious stones with his foot. </p><br><p>Many people were entering that church. After they left, the patriarch entered that church. He saw that the gold and the precious gems had been damaged by the foot of that man. The patriarch was terrified and angry. He departed in great indignation. </p><br><p>He said to the people: “Don’t go away. Turn back. Who is it who has damaged the church?”</p><br><p>But that man was weeping near the icon of Mary so that the people would not recognize him.</p><br><p>The patriarch said to the people: “Each one of you, turn back.”</p><br><p>And all of the people turned back, each and every one. That man also remained [inside the church]. He prostrated himself in front of the icon of Mary. He was drenched with tears and his foot of stone was broken. He became like other people.</p><br><p>When the people saw him, they declared him blessed. They also bowed to the icon of Mary.</p><br><p>Then the patriarch beckoned to that man, saying to him: “When did you become like this?”</p><br><p>The man said to the patriarch: “I was like this since I came out of my mother’s womb. When I recognized [my affliction], I concealed it with cloth, so that people would not recognize me. I continued like this, weeping, evening and morning, day and night, all the time. I was prostrating myself in front of the icon of Mary and was visiting the church. But whenever I entered the church, the gold and the jacinth were crushed. Moreover, you were enraged against all the people because of my error. You told the people: ‘Turn back to the church, each and every one of you.’ So the lot came to me, and I remained alone so that I could visit the church. I was afraid and I prostrated myself in front of the icon of Mary. I wept and then my foot of stone was broken.”</p><br><p>Having heard this, the patriarch was amazed. He himself went and prostrated in front of the icon of Mary. Then he rose, lifted his eyes, and asked God about this miracle of Mary. </p><br><p>My dear blessed Lady, the Blessed of God, the Mother of the Maker of all creation, will you transform me with your compassion and your mercy? My dear Lady, Mother of the Lord, do not abandon me into nothingness. I would be lost. My dear Lady, do not turn your face away from me, so that I would not be lost in vain. My dear Lady, the Mother of the Creator, look at me with eyes of mercy. My dear Lady, the Untearable Curtain of the Sanctuary, turn your ear to my prayer and petition. My dear Lady, Mother of my Lord, who reigns forever and ever, also save me from the devil, assail the ill spirit of sin, expel it from me. Fashion in me a holy spirit that lives forever inside of me. My dear Lady, deliver me from the noonday demon and from forces that move in darkness. My dear Lady, all the time my enemies want me to die and they would kill me if your Son did not protect me with his compassion and his mercy. My dear Lady, mother of my Lord, my enemies who oppose my soul are many. Mother of my Lord, intercede for me, ask your excellent son, Our Savior, for mercy on my behalf. Ask that he show mercy to us, forgive our sins and wipe out the account of our sins by the prayer of Our Lady, the Mother of God and by the prayer of Steven, the first martyr, and the prayer of George, the wonderworker. Dear Lord, remember the soul of your maidservant Batra Aron and its scribe Farikahen when you come into your kingdom in this world and in the world to come. Forever and ever amen.</p><br>"
