    "incipit": "ዘከመ፡ አስተርአየቶ፡ ለአባ፡ ሳሙኤል፡ ዘደብረ፡ ቀልሞን፡ አመ፡ ወሰድዎ፡ በርባር፡ ወተመይጠ። ጸሎታ፡…. ወእምዝ፡ ወሰድዎ፡ ሰብኣ፡ በርባር፡ ለአባ፡ ሳሙኤል፡ ዘቀልሞን፡ ኀበ፡ ሀገሮሙ",
    "manuscript_count": 44,
    "translations": [
      {
        "author": "Elliot Galvis",
        "text": "<p>I [Saint John] say to you, oh Prochorus my son, I saw Christ the Lord embrace the sheets lying over his mother’s body many times, with all the saints watching and seeing him cradle [her body], and saying to his mother: “Peace to you, oh my mother, a beautiful island beloved before those of heaven and earth. Peace to my mother, in whom, second Heaven, I dwelled on Earth. Peace to my mother who is higher and better than all the sons of men [conceived] from sexual union. Peace to the glorious throne on which I sat, to these, her pure arms. Peace to the paradise, the sweet fruits of which no one partook except me, the milk in her breast. And just as you bore me, oh my virgin mother, look–delight now in this peaceful place for eternity. And just as you took on frailties and pains in your body upon the Earth, take up in their place unending joy for eternity in Heaven. </p><p></p><p>“If you were downtrodden in your body on Earth, rise now to ascend with me into the heavens. If you, in this body on Earth, went with me to Egypt and carried me in your arms, rise now, and I will lead you into the highest heaven among the cherubic order. And if you hungered in body, my truly beloved mother, look, I will take you up into a house of joys and delights for eternity. And look, if your heart was ever full of fear for me in your body, while you were fleeing [pregnant] with me from place to place, rise now into a place of quiet in Jerusalem, my favorite city [excelsam civitatem meam; lit. “my most elevated state”], where [there is] no sadness or heartache. And if your eyes were full with lament and sadness, when you, weeping, were beyond the wall outside [Jerusalem], look now: the kythira-playing cherub will sing openly before you in the heavens.” </p><p>And the Savior said these things in order to comfort the body of his virgin mother. </p><p>[Translation as of 05/21/22]</p>"
      },
      {
        "author": "Rowan Williams",
        "text": "<p>The Miracles of Our Lady Mary, the Holy Twofold Virgin Theotokos</p><p>May her prayers and blessings be with us to the ages of ages. Amen.</p><p> </p><p>This is how John, the Son of Thunder, related what he saw when he venerated the shroud which was upon Our Lady Mary, the holy twofold Virgin Theotokos.[1] He said, ‘I saw Our Lord Jesus Christ venerating the shroud which was upon her many times. 3When all the Saints saw that, they marvelled at the words of comfort which He spoke to His Mother, saying, “Salutation to you, My Mother and Birth-giver! You are the chosen, beautiful oasis, which is greater than all those in Heaven and those on Earth. 4Salutation to the boat in which I dwelt for nine months. 5Salutation to My Mother Mary, the second Heaven in which I dwelt on Earth. 6Salutation to My Mother, who is more exalted than all the children of humankind. 7Salutation to the throne of glory on which I was seated, 8that is, the arms of My pure Mother.[2] 9Salutation to you, the garden whose sweet fruits none have taken apart from Me, that is, your speech-endowing milk.[3] 10As you suffered with Me, My Virgin Mother, behold, you shall rejoice now in the places of rest for ever. 11As you bore suffering and weariness in your body with Me on Earth, receive joy in their place for ever in the Kingdom of Heaven. 12Although you have been buried in the earth bodily, you will rise up now and ascend with Me into Heaven. 13Although you travelled with Me to the lands of Egypt and Ethiopia in this body, which bore Me in your arms, you will rise up now, and I shall take you to the high Heavens where the ranks of the Cherubim reside. 14Although you experienced hunger in the body, My truly beloved Mother, behold, I shall translate you[4] to the land of joy and gladness for ever. 15Although while you were with Me your heart was filled with dismay in this body and fled with Me from place to place, behold, you shall rise up now and go to the place of rest in Jerusalem, My city on high, where there is no suffering or death, no sadness or toil. 16And although your eyes were filled with tears and sadness and you are in this tomb, outside which people weep,[5] behold, now the lutes of the Cherubim will play before you in Heaven.” 17Having said this, the Saviour comforted the body of His Virgin Mother.</p><p>18   The greatness of her honour is very wonderful, and her glory is marvellous. When she ascended in the body,[6] her Son venerated her.[7]</p><p>May her prayers and blessings be with us to the ages of ages. Amen.</p>"
      }
    ]
