    "id": "1138",
    "title": "King Menelik (Menilek) II, the 19th c. Ethiopian monarch, and his reign and how the candelabra of the Church of Aksum Seyon Maryam miraculously lights up in 1896",
    "incipit": "ስምዑ፡ ሰብአ፡ ኢትዮጵያ፡ እለ። ታፈቅርዋ፡ ለምነ። ጽዮን፡ ዘአክሱም። ዘኮነ፡ ተአምረ፡ ወመንክረ፡ በ፲ወ፰፻ወ፺ወ፮ዓመተ፡ ምሕረት፡ በመዋዕለ፡ መንግሥቱ። ለንጉሥነ። ዳግማዊ፡ ምኒልክ፡ መዋዔ፡ ፀር፡ ወበመዋዕለ። ሢመቱ፡ ለንቡረ፡ ዕድ፡ ወልደ፡ ጊዮርጊስ። ርቱዓ፡ ሃይማኖት፡ ዓመ፡ ፳ሁ። ለሕዳር፡ ተጋብኡ፡ ካህናት፡ ዘገበዘ፡ አክሱም፡ ሕዝብ። ቅዱሳን፡ ደቂቀ። ጽዮን፡ ውሉደ፡ መርዓ፡ ፍሡኃን።",
    "manuscript_count": 4,
    "translations": [
      {
        "author": "Mehari Worku with Wendy Laura Belcher",
        "text": "<p>A miracle [performed] by Our Lady Mary, the Holy Two-fold Virgin, the Mother of God, may her prayer and blessings be with us, forever and ever, amen. </p><p></p><p>A rich man, who neither feared the Lord nor did good for the poor and the church, had a son who was a bishop in a certain city. </p><p>The son used to advise his father, and rebuke him, saying, “Father, fear the Lord’s judgment. Avoid evil and be distant from sinning!” </p><p>His father, however, didn’t listen to him. Rather, he did more wicked things and piled up his sins. He completed his days in rebellion and debauchery, and when he died, the angels of darkness took his soul to Sheol.</p><p>The bishop became distressed for his father. For the bishop was a saintly man and loved his father. He mourned him greatly.</p><p>He implored the Lord with much fasting and prayer vigils to show him where his father was and what had happened to him after his death.</p><p>The Lord’s angel came to the bishop in a dream and gave him a tour of all the places of condemnation [in Sheol]. One of the places was a deep and wide pit. That fiery pit was filled to the brim with darkness. From it, came smoke and sulfur with a very disgusting and repulsive stench.</p><p>The bishop was astonished and asked the angel about this terrifying and petrifying place.</p><p>The angel answered, “This is the place called Gehenna. All the evil rich people who neither show mercy to the poor nor help their neighbors dwell in this pit. Those here completed their days with rebellion, violence, and debauchery, dying without repentance.”</p><p>When the bishop heard this, he became despondent and wept bitterly.</p><p>Waking up from his sleep, he took every possession that his father left to him and shared them with the poor and the needy.</p><p>He also fasted and prayed, doing this for forty days in the church and imploring the Lord with many tears and sighs.</p><p>The angel [again] came to him in dream and took him to the place where his father was. The bishop saw his father and his shoulder to his head were out of the pit. From his shoulders downwards, however, he was in the pit of damnation.</p><p>When the bishop woke up from his sleep, he increased his fasting, asceticism, and prayer vigils. He celebrated the Eucharist every day for six months. </p><p>Again, the angel came and took him to where his father was and showed him. Behold, the bishop saw his father was out of the pit of damnation all the way up to his waist. But, below his waist he was in damnation.</p><p>At that time, the bishop cried out and said, “Dear father, isn’t this what I was afraid would happen to you? Is this what advised you to avoid? But, you didn’t want to listen to me!”</p><p>His father replied, “My dear son, hurry to save me from this bitter damnation. Increase your fasting and prayer, don’t stop giving alms, and celebrate the Eucharist for my sake. For it is by your prayer and the Body and Blood of Christ that half of my soul is delivered from damnation.”</p><p>While the bishop standing in the [place] of his father’s damnation, he woke up. He increased his fasting and prayer vigils, wearing sackcloth and ashes. He celebrated the Eucharist every day for six more months without ceasing. </p><p>Then, again, he had a dream. This time, Our Lord Jesus Christ came down to that place and ordered the angel to take the father’s soul out and bring her to him.</p><p>When the angel brought her, Christ said, “I have forgiven this soul because of this bishop’s toiling labor, wholehearted prayer, and for the sake of [his father’s name being mentioned when] my Body and Blood [are celebrated].” </p><p>Then Christ washed the father’s soul with the Water of Life and ushered her into the paradise of joy.</p><p>When the bishop woke up, he joyfully rejoiced, praising the Lord and thanking Our Lady Mary, the Holy Two-Fold Virgin, the Mother of God.</p><p>We too should ask the Lord to forgive our sins and make us worthy of his kingdom through </p><p>the prayer and supplication to Our Lady Mary, the Bridge of All Prayers [to the Lord], </p><p>the prayer of John the Baptizer, the Star of the Wildernesses and Desert, and </p><p>the prayer of Stephen, the first martyr and the archdeacon, and</p><p>the prayer of the whole gathering of the saints and martyrs.</p><p></p><p>May her prayer and her blessing be with us, forever and ever. Amen. </p>"
      }
    ]
