    "title": "Kings Abraha and Atsbaha (Abraha and Atsbeha) and Fruementius: Part 2: How the Virgin Mary helps Fruementius (Abba Selama) go to Lake Tana during the 300s to baptize the people and the kings",
    "incipit": "ወእም ፡  አመ ፡  ሢመተ ፡  ጵጵስናሁ ፡  ለአባ ፡  ሰላማ ፡  ከሣቴ ፡  ብርሃን ፡  በሠለስቱ ፡  ዓመት ፡  ወሠለስቱ ፡  አውራኅ ፡  እንዘ ፡  ሀሎ ፡  ውስተ ፡  ብሔረ ፡  አክሱም ፡  አስተርአየቶ ፡  እግዝእትነ ፡  ... ወትቤሎ ፡  ሑር ፡  ውስተ ፡  ደሴተ ፡  ጣና ፡  ወበህየ ፡  ታጠምቅ ፡  ወትሜህሮሙ ፡  ሃይማኖተ ፡  ክርስትና። ወንግሮሙ ፡  ለአብርሃ ፡  ወአጽብሐ ፡  ነገሥታተ ፡  ኢትዮጵያ ፡  ጻድቃን ፡  ወኄራን ፡  ይሑሩ ፡  ምስሌከ ፡  ምስለ ፡  ሠራዊቶሙ።",
    "manuscript_count": 4,
    "translations": [
      {
        "author": "Rowan Williams",
        "text": "<p>The Miracles of Our Lady Mary, the Holy Twofold Virgin Theotokos</p><p>May her prayers and blessings be with us to the ages of ages. Amen.</p><p>Now there was a certain man of the tribe of Shem, the son of Noah, whose name was Abraham, the good and righteous friend of the Lord who loved guests and sojourners. He pleased the Lord in all his ways, and the name of his wife was Sarah. 3These holy people kept the laws of the Trinity and welcomed guests and sojourners. 4And without guests, they would not eat or drink anything, even as much as a mustard seed.</p><p>5   Now when Satan, the hater of good things, saw this, he was jealous of him, and he sent one of his minions, saying, 6‘Go and sit on the road to Midian[1] and speak falsehood with convincing proofs so that guests might not go to the tent of Abraham. 7Pound your head with a rock now, until your blood flows like water on the ground.’ 8Upon hearing these words, the demon went down to Midian, took a rock and split open his head, to such an extent that his blood flowed down to the ground, and having done this, he sat at the side of the road. 9Then certain wayfarers came to him, and this hater of the good said to them, ‘Greetings, my fellow wayfarers! Where have you come from? And where are you going?’ 10The wayfarers told him, ‘We are going to the tent of a good man called Abraham.’ 11So the demon said, ‘Have you not heard that Abraham is an evil man? 12Come and see how he split open my head,[2]  to the end that my blood flowed like water because of his hatred of guests. Do not go to him, lest what befell me happens to you.’ 13Then the wayfarers said to one another, ‘What has made Abraham do evil when he is a good man?’ 14And as they discussed this, they turned around and went back to their own land. 15That day Abraham waited, but he could find no guests, 16so he went home and slept without tasting anything.</p><p>17   The next day, as five men travelled towards him, the demon met them and spoke to them as he had before, saying, ‘O men of this world, where are you going?’ 18‘We are going to the tent of Abraham,’ they responded. 19‘Look upon me, my brothers,’ he said to them, ‘Come and see my blood gushing forth from the middle of my head. Abraham has split open the crown of my head. 20Return in peace to your own country now, lest you become like me.’ 21Then the travellers said to one another, ‘It is best for us to return to our own country, lest Abraham kill us.’ 22Again Abraham waited for travellers along the road until sunset,[3] but he found none. 23So he went into his tent and slept without tasting anything. </p><p>   24   On the third day, the Trinity, the Rulers of the world, saw the strength of Abraham’s heart and the works of Satan, and They went to the tent of that good man together.[4] 25At that time the counsel of Satan was brought to nothing. They seized him and cast him into the abyss of Sheol below. 26And when Abraham lifted up his eyes at the sixth hour of the day, he saw Three Men standing before him.[5] He looked and ran from the entrance to his tent to welcome Them. Then he bowed down to the ground. 27And he said to Them, ‘My Lord, if I have found favour in Your eyes, let us bring water to wash Your feet, that You may take shelter under the tree. Let us bring bread that You may eat, and after that You can go where You plan to go, since You have turned aside to Your servant.’ 28And the Holy Trinity said to him, ‘Do what you plan to do, as you have said.’ 29So Abraham hurried over to his wife Sarah in her tent and said to her, ‘Quickly, kneed three measures of wheat and make unleavened bread.’ 30Then Abraham went to the herd, took a calf and gave it to his servant, who slaughtered it quickly and prepared it. 31After that, he brought out yoghurt and honey with the calf which he had prepared and served it to Them. They ate, and he stood by the tree, showing them hospitality.[6] 32Then the Lord said to Abraham, ‘I shall return to you at this time next year. Sarah will have a son, and you will call his name Isaac. I shall establish My covenant with you and his seed his seed after him as an eternal covenant.[7] Nations and kings of peoples will go forth from her, for I shall bless her and grant her sons from you.’ 33Abraham fell on his face and laughed, saying in his heart,[8] ‘Shall I, a hundred-year-old man, beget a son? And will Sarah give birth when she is ninety years old?’ 34God said to Abraham, ‘Is anything impossible for the Lord? When I return to you at this time, in the seventh month, Sarah will have a son as I have said to you.’ 35Moreover, the Lord said to Abraham, ‘Behold, I shall establish My covenant between Me and you. I shall greatly increase your descendants[9] as the sand of the sea and the stars of the sky; I shall make kings and nations go forth from you.’</p><p>36   After that, the Lord visited Sarah as He had said. She conceived and gave birth to a son, and Abraham named the child Isaac. 37So the child grew and was weaned. And Abraham made a great feast on the day Isaac was weaned. 38And they praised the glorious Lord Whose word is inviolable.[10]</p><p>39   My brothers and sisters, concerning whom did the Lord say to Abraham, ‘I shall return to you at this time next year’? Was it not concerning Our Lady Mary, she who went forth from the root of Adam and the loins of Noah and passed into the house of Abraham, the father of many nations? For her sake, the Trinity were shown hospitality in the tent of Abraham, to announce the Incarnation of the Son of God from the seed of Abraham. 40Therefore, it is fitting for us to know and understand that the Lord showed signs of the Nativity of Our Lady at diverse and sundry times.[11] </p><p>May her prayers and blessings be with us to the ages of ages. Amen.</p>"
      }
    ]
