      {
        "author": "Jeremy Brown & Dawit Muluneh with Wendy Laura Belcher",
        "text": "<p>A miracle performed by our Lady Mary, the Twofold Virgin, Sweet of Name, Mother of God, may her prayer and her blessing be with the soul of … and with … our father Walda Selassie, forever and ever amen.</p><p></p><p>It is said about a [certain] hyena that she bore two cubs and those young hyenas’ eyes were blind. </p><p></p><p>[At that time,] a monk was living in the midst of the wilderness with the wild animals. The icon of our Lady Mary, the holy two-fold Virgin, sweet of name, mother of God, stayed in that monk’s hand [all day].</p><p> </p><p>Right away, [after giving birth,] the hyena brought the two blind cubs and dropped them on the monk’s doorstep.</p><p></p><p>The monk understood [what she needed] and petitioned that icon of Our Lady Mary, the holy two-fold Virgin, sweet of name, mother of God [to help them]. </p><p></p><p>Mary opened the hyena cubs’ eyes through the power of her prayer. </p><p></p><p>Afterwards, the hyena cubs went away with their mother. </p><p></p><p>As the hyena went searching for food, according to her habit, she found a sheepskin and brought it [to give] to that monk.</p><p></p><p>May her prayer and blessing, and the mercy of her beloved son be with … forever and ever, amen.</p>"
      }
